/*
 * Not decoration. The OFL requires its text to travel with the font, and
 * THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md states that it does in every bundle -- this site
 * serves the font, so this site is a bundle and owes the notice.
 *
 * The table mirrors THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md section by section: what ships in
 * a plugin or a module, and nothing that only builds or tests it.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/paths.js';

const REPO = 'https://github.com/graebe/neon-ingvy-audio-plugins';
---
<Base title="Licences" description="GPL-3.0-or-later, and the third-party notices that travel with it.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Licences</p>
  <h1>GPL-3.0-or-later, with every notice it carries</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Everything in this repository is <strong>GPL-3.0-or-later</strong>,
      Copyright (C) 2026 Torben Gräber: free software you may redistribute and
      modify under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your
      option) any later version, with no warranty. The full text is
      <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>LICENSE</a>, and it ships inside
      every plugin and every module.
    </p>

    <p>
      Every release links the source it was built from: the release notes name
      the tag, and the tag's tree is the whole source of that build. GPLv3
      gives everyone who receives a plugin or a module that right.
    </p>

    <h2>What ships with it</h2>

    <p>
      Each dependency keeps its own notice, because a permissive licence's
      conditions travel with the copy rather than being replaced by ours. The
      full notices are in
      <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md`}>THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md</a>,
      which ships beside <code>LICENSE</code>; this is the shape of it.
    </p>

    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>this repository</td><td><strong>GPL-3.0-or-later</strong>, © 2026 Torben Gräber — the engines, the shells, the editors and the modules</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/iPlug2/iPlug2">iPlug2</a></td><td><strong>zlib</strong>, with the parts of WDL it compiles in (zlib); its IGraphics and standalone-app libraries are linked into nothing that ships</td></tr>
        <tr><td>VST3 SDK</td><td><strong>MIT</strong>, © 2026 Steinberg Media Technologies GmbH</td></tr>
        <tr><td>CLAP, clap-helpers</td><td><strong>MIT</strong>, © 2021 Alexandre Bique</td></tr>
        <tr><td>JSON for Modern C++</td><td><strong>MIT</strong>, © Niels Lohmann, compiled in by iPlug2's WebView editor; its Hedley header is <strong>CC0-1.0</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>the Rust standard library</td><td><strong>MIT OR Apache-2.0</strong>, in every plugin and every module, distributed here under MIT</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rust crates from crates.io</td><td>each under a licence on the allowlist below; THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md lists every one that ships, with its notice</td></tr>
        <tr><td>solid-js</td><td><strong>MIT</strong>, bundled into every editor</td></tr>
        <tr><td>vite's module-preload polyfill</td><td><strong>MIT</strong>, a few hundred bytes at the top of every editor's script; the rest of vite is a build tool and ships in nothing</td></tr>
        <tr><td>JetBrains Mono</td><td><strong>SIL OFL 1.1</strong> — this site serves <a href={url('fonts/OFL.txt')}>OFL.txt</a> with the font, and each plugin bundle carries it in <code>Contents/Resources/web/fonts/</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>NI Side-Chain's MIDI trigger</td><td>ported from <a href="https://github.com/charlesvestal/schwung-ducker">schwung-ducker</a>, <strong>MIT</strong>, © 2026 Charles Vestal — a port is a derivative work, so its notice stays beside ours</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>How they combine</h2>

    <p>
      Every licence above is one GPLv3 can take in: MIT, zlib, Apache-2.0 and
      the OFL ask for their notices to travel, and they do. A Rust crate is
      linked only if its licence is on the allowlist — MIT, Apache-2.0,
      BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Zlib, MPL-2.0, Unicode-3.0, CC0-1.0,
      Unlicense or GPL-3.0. Nothing else is, GPL-2.0-only included: it cannot
      be combined with GPLv3.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>JUCE 9</strong>, the shell that replaces iPlug2, is
      <strong>AGPLv3</strong>. GPLv3's section 13 allows a GPLv3 work to be
      combined with an AGPLv3 one and the result conveyed: our part stays
      under GPLv3, and AGPLv3's own section 13, on interaction through a
      network, applies to the combination as such.
    </p>

    <p>
      Until 2026-10-06 this repository was MIT, and that goal decided the
      shell, the editor and the dependencies.
      <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/adr/0001-gpl-3.0-or-later.md`}>The decision record</a>
      says what it cost and why it changed.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .eyebrow { display: block; margin-bottom: var(--s3); }
  h1 { margin-bottom: var(--s6); }
</style>
